"[2509.24591] PoseDiff: A Unified Diffusion Model Bridging Robot Pose Estimation and Video-to-Action Control (https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.24591)\nciteturn3674view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.24591\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Robotics\nL7: \nL8: This paper has been withdrawn by Haozhuo Zhang\nL9: \nL10: [Submitted on 29 Sep 2025 (cite5†v1 ), last revised 30 Oct 2025 (this version, v2)]\nL11: # Title:PoseDiff: A Unified Diffusion Model Bridging Robot Pose Estimation and Video-to-Action Control\nL12: \nL13: Authors:cite6†Haozhuo Zhang , cite7†Michele Caprio , cite8†Jing Shao , cite9†Qiang Zhang , cite10†Jian Tang , cite11†Shanghang Zhang , cite12†Wei Pan L14: \nL15: View a PDF of the paper titled PoseDiff: A Unified Diffusion Model Bridging Robot Pose Estimation and Video-to-Action Control, by Haozhuo Zhang and 6 other authors\nL16: \nL17: cite13†No PDF available, click to view other formats L18: > Abstract:We present PoseDiff, a conditional diffusion model that unifies robot state estimation and control within a single framework. At its core, PoseDiff maps raw visual observations into structured robot states-such as 3D keypoints or joint angles-from a single RGB image, eliminating the need for multi-stage pipelines or auxiliary modalities.\nL19: Building upon this foundation, PoseDiff extends naturally to video-to-action inverse dynamics: by conditioning on sparse video keyframes generated by world models, it produces smooth and continuous long-horizon action sequences through an overlap-averaging strategy. This unified design enables scalable and efficient integration of perception and control. On the DREAM dataset, PoseDiff achieves state-of-the-art accuracy and real-time performance for pose estimation.\nL20: On Libero-Object manipulation tasks, it substantially improves success rates over existing inverse dynamics modules, even under strict offline settings. Together, these results show that PoseDiff provides a scalable, accurate, and efficient bridge between perception, planning, and control in embodied AI. The video visualization results can be found on the project page: cite14†this https URL†haozhuo-zhang.github.io .\nL21: Comments:  | The experimental setup and metrics lacks rigor, affecting the fairness of the comparisons\nL22: Subjects:  | Robotics (cs.RO); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL23: Cite as:  | cite15†arXiv:2509.24591 [cs.RO]\nL24:    | (or cite16†arXiv:2509.24591v2 [cs.RO] for this version)\nL25:    | cite17†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2509.24591†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL26: ## Submission history\nL27: \nL28: From: Haozhuo Zhang [cite18†view email ]\nL29: cite5†[v1] Mon, 29 Sep 2025 10:55:48 UTC (6,605 KB)\nL30: [v2] Thu, 30 Oct 2025 15:48:32 UTC (1 KB) (withdrawn)\nL31: \nL32: Full-text links:\nL33: \nL34: ## Access Paper:\nL35: \nL36: View a PDF of the paper titled PoseDiff: A Unified Diffusion Model Bridging Robot Pose Estimation and Video-to-Action Control, by Haozhuo Zhang and 6 other authors\nL37: \nL38:   * Withdrawn\nL39: \nL40: No license for this version due to withdrawn\nL41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: cs.RO\nL44: \nL45: cite19†< prev |   cite20†next > L46: \nL47: cite21†new | cite22†recent | cite23†2025-09 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite24†cs L52: cite25†cs.AI L53: \nL54: ### References & Citations\nL55: \nL56:   * cite26†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L57:   * cite27†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L58:   * cite28†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L59: \nL60: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading